WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.280
With his eye-catching good&nbsp;
looks and magnetic aura,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:08.640
it’s no surprise why Jason Momoa has charmed so&nbsp;
many film and television viewers. He achieved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.360
stupendous silver screen success by playing&nbsp;
Aquaman in the blockbuster of the same name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.240
which is the second-highest-grossing DC Extended&nbsp;
Universe movie as of the making of this video.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:24.240
Momoa also gained acclaim for his performance as&nbsp;
the charismatic Duncan Idaho in the 2021 sci-fi&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.440
epic "Dune." He will portray the Protector of the&nbsp;
Deep for the second time in "Aquaman and the Lost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.640
Kingdom," which Momoa praised for being more&nbsp;
lighthearted than its darker DCEU counterparts.

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:38.240
Before he was a big box office draw,&nbsp;
Momoa was best known for his role on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:44.320
TV's preeminent fantasy show. He appeared as&nbsp;
the menacing and memorable Dothraki leader&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.040
Khal Drogo during the first season and one&nbsp;
episode of the second season of "Game of Thrones."

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.960
In the series premiere "Winter is Coming,"&nbsp;
Drogo enters an arranged marriage with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.360
Daenerys Targaryen, played by Emilia Clarke.&nbsp;
The two eventually fall in love, but their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:01.760
relationship is marred in the beginning&nbsp;
by disturbing non-consensual sex acts.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.280
While filming these graphic and&nbsp;
disagreeable so-called love scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.800
Momoa did everything in his power to&nbsp;
make his co-star comfortable. Since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.760
he was so considerate towards her, Clarke has&nbsp;
publicly praised Momoa for his on-set behavior.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:18.240
"Game of Thrones" has been heralded as one of the&nbsp;
greatest shows of all time, but that adulation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:22.960
has not shielded it from criticism. Viewers and&nbsp;
critics have called out the HBO series for its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:27.680
gratuitous sex and nudity. Emilia Clarke appeared&nbsp;
in numerous nude scenes in the first season&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:32.320
of "Game of Thrones," oftentimes without any&nbsp;
clear plot-related reason to justify the stunt.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.760
Since the actress was 23 with only&nbsp;
a few acting credits to her name,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.480
she was understandably uneasy not wearing clothes&nbsp;
on set. To make matters worse, Clarke's first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:45.280
intimate scene on "Game of Thrones" involved her&nbsp;
character being sexually assaulted by her husband.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:49.600
While filming the upsetting scene with her&nbsp;
castmate, Jason Momoa, he did his best to make her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.160
feel at ease and protected, which is what every&nbsp;
young actor deserves from their scene partners.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:58.240
Clarke told the "Armchair Expert" podcast&nbsp;
that Momoa "took care of her" and "was so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.320
kind and considerate" toward her. She added&nbsp;
that he demanded the crew give her a robe to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:07.040
cover up and keep warm between takes. Clarke's&nbsp;
account of Momoa's on-set behavior proves what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:11.680
a warmhearted and thoughtful performer he is.&nbsp;
It's a personality trait that shines through,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.120
even when he's playing a ruthless&nbsp;
character like the Dothraki khal.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.280
Jason Momoa's sweet and supportive behavior&nbsp;
towards Emilia Clarke extended beyond their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:23.760
intimate scenes. The "Aquaman" actor was&nbsp;
incredibly concerned about his "GOT" co-star's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.320
health. In a beautifully candid and courageous&nbsp;
essay in The New Yorker, Clarke opened up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:32.640
about her potentially fatal brain aneurysms.&nbsp;
The same year "Game of Thrones" premiered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.760
she experienced a subarachnoid hemorrhage. Clarke&nbsp;
also had an operation to treat a life-threatening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:42.240
brain bleed caused by a second aneurysm&nbsp;
two years after the first one ruptured.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.160
When Entertainment Tonight asked Momoa about&nbsp;
Clarke's health issues, he revealed he had,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.000
quote, "kind of been a part of that&nbsp;
whole situation for a very long time." He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.680
added that he was "trying to find the right&nbsp;
way to come out and help" after Clarke's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:58.880
health scares. Momoa said he was sad because the&nbsp;
world "almost lost her numerous times." He also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:03.120
emphasized that he loves the Mother of Dragons&nbsp;
portrayer and that she will do great things.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.920
"It's very sad, because we almost&nbsp;
lost her numerous times. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.280
I love her to bits and she's here and&nbsp;
she's going to do great things with it."

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:16.000
It is clear the former on-screen spouses share&nbsp;
a profound emotional bond. They remain close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.920
about a decade after they met on the "GOT"&nbsp;
set. According to Entertainment Weekly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:24.800
Momoa and Clarke reunited in August 2021&nbsp;
at David Benioff's birthday party. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.120
took adorable photos together, one of which&nbsp;
Momoa posted on Instagram with the caption,

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.840
"MOON OF MY LIFE. you are&nbsp;
wonderful love u forever."

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.600
If you or anyone you know has&nbsp;
been a victim of sexual assault,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.640
help is available. Visit the Rape, Abuse &amp;&nbsp;
Incest National Network website or contact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:45.840
RAINN's National Helpline&nbsp;
at 1-800-656-HOPE (4673).

